{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1790897236156,"sessionID":"ses_f06353c07ffegrxTCvX2CYLafu","part":{"id":"prt_0f9cb28b80018fHTMLSAla1CRV","messageID":"msg_0f9cb152b001VaUqP0LOh4qzsu","sessionID":"ses_f06353c07ffegrxTCvX2CYLafu","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1790897275640,"sessionID":"ses_f06353c07ffegrxTCvX2CYLafu","part":{"id":"prt_0f9cb9d2f00181tql2m6ZtVAPk","messageID":"msg_0f9cb152b001VaUqP0LOh4qzsu","sessionID":"ses_f06353c07ffegrxTCvX2CYLafu","type":"text","text":"I now have all the operative code. Here's what the source shows:\n\n**Key rotation & signing:** `Signer.secret_keys` stores the list \"from oldest to newest. The newest (last) key is used for signing.\" `get_signature` calls `key = self.derive_key()`, and `derive_key` defaults `secret_key` to `self.secret_keys[-1]` — so the newest (last) key signs.\n\n**Primary verification:** `Signer.verify_signature` iterates `for secret_key in reversed(self.secret_keys)` — newest-first.\n\n**Fallback signers:** `Serializer.iter_unsigners` yields the primary signer first, then for each fallback config does `for secret_key in self.secret_keys: yield fallback(secret_key, ...)` — oldest-first, in given list order — and `loads` iterates those signers in that order.","time":{"start":1790897265967,"end":1790897275639}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790897275652,"sessionID":"ses_f06353c07ffegrxTCvX2CYLafu","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"rehearsal_submit_answer","callID":"call_f6ed576d2eb646b58d2cf110","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"answer":{"fallback_key_order":{"citations":[{"path":"src/itsdangerous/serializer.py","quote":"        yield self.make_signer(salt)\n\n        for fallback in self.fallback_signers:\n            if isinstance(fallback, dict):\n                kwargs = fallback\n                fallback = self.signer\n            elif isinstance(fallback, tuple):\n                fallback, kwargs = fallback\n            else:\n                kwargs = self.signer_kwargs\n\n            for secret_key in self.secret_keys:\n                yield fallback(secret_key, salt=salt, **kwargs)"},{"path":"src/itsdangerous/serializer.py","quote":"        #: The list of secret keys to try for verifying signatures, from\n        #: oldest to newest. The newest (last) key "},{"path":"src/itsdangerous/signer.py","quote":"    #: The list of secret keys to try for verifying signatures, from\n    #: oldest to newest. The newest (last) key is used for signing."}],"value":"oldest-first"},"primary_before_fallback":{"citations":[{"path":"src/itsdangerous/serializer.py","quote":"        \"\"\"Iterates over all signers to be tried for unsigning. Starts\n        with the configured signer, then constructs each signer\n        specified in ``fallback_signers``.\n        \"\"\"\n        if salt is None:\n            salt = self.salt\n\n        yield self.make_signer(salt)"},{"path":"src/itsdangerous/serializer.py","quote":"        s = want_bytes(s)\n        last_exception = None\n\n        for signer in self.iter_unsigners(salt):\n            try:\n                return self.load_payload(signer.unsign(s))\n            except BadSignature as err:\n                last_exception = err"}],"value":true},"primary_verification_key_order":{"citations":[{"path":"src/itsdangerous/signer.py","quote":"        for secret_key in reversed(self.secret_keys):\n            key = self.derive_key(secret_key)\n\n            if self.algorithm.verify_signature(key, value, sig):\n                return True"},{"path":"src/itsdangerous/signer.py","quote":"        #: The list of secret keys to try for verifying signatures, from\n        #: oldest to newest. The newest (last) key is used for signing."}],"value":"newest-first"},"signing_key_position":{"citations":[{"path":"src/itsdangerous/signer.py","quote":"        #: The list of secret keys to try for verifying signatures, from\n        #: oldest to newest. The newest (last) key is used for signing.\n        #:\n        #: This allows a key rotation system to keep a list of allowed\n        #: keys and remove expired ones.\n        self.secret_keys: list[bytes] = _make_keys_list(secret_key)"},{"path":"src/itsdangerous/signer.py","quote":"        if secret_key is None:\n            secret_key = self.secret_keys[-1]"},{"path":"src/itsdangerous/signer.py","quote":"        value = want_bytes(value)\n        key = self.derive_key()\n        sig = self.algorithm.get_signature(key, value)"},{"path":"src/itsdangerous/serializer.py","quote":"    @property\n    def secret_key(self) -> bytes:\n        \"\"\"The newest (last) entry in the :attr:`secret_keys` list. This\n        is for compatibility from before key rotation support was added.\n        \"\"\"\n        return self.secret_keys[-1]"}],"value":"last"}}},"output":"{\"submitted\":true}","metadata":{"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1790897275638,"end":1790897275642}},"id":"prt_0f9cbc2f2001aGGz7hfLWS3i7F","sessionID":"ses_f06353c07ffegrxTCvX2CYLafu","messageID":"msg_0f9cb152b001VaUqP0LOh4qzsu"}}
